                    round2_briefing:     `<b>THE DECISION: PAY OR REBUILD?</b><br><br>Forensic analysis is complete. The hacker (Nerovane group) was inside the network for 3 weeks before encrypting. 500GB of data (11 years of records) were exfiltrated.<br><br><b>Path A — Pay Ransom ($450K + $25K Bitcoin fee):</b> System online in ~48 hours. Nerovane has ~80% track record of delivering decryption keys. Risk of residual malware and legal exposure.<br><br><b>Path B — Rebuild from Backup:</b> 4-6 weeks to full operation. Cost: $2M-$3M direct + $4M-$5M lost revenue. Cleaner and more secure, but devastating downtime.<br><br><b>Path C — Hybrid:</b> Pay ransom AND rebuild/verify in parallel. The most expensive path, and it carries the risks of both.<br><br>Choose your path and allocate your budget.`,
                    round2_budget_label: `Additional Budget Allocation ($K)`,
                    round2_budget_hint:  `Range: $0K to $5,000K. For rebuild or hybrid, higher budget improves data recovery.`,
                    round2_strategy_label: `Ransom Decision`,
                    round2_opt1: "Pay the ransom — $475K in total, systems back in about 48 hours",
                    round2_opt2: "Rebuild from the 11-day backup — 4 to 6 weeks to full operations",
                    round2_opt3: "Hybrid — pay the ransom and rebuild in parallel to verify the restored data",

                    round3_briefing:     `<b>LEGAL AND REGULATORY RESPONSE</b><br><br>The crisis is being managed, but stakeholders are demanding answers.<br><br><b>Regulador (Banco Central de Honduras):</b> Requires security incident notification within 48 hours. Can impose fines of 0.5%-2% of capital ($150K-$600K). If ransom was paid, potential AML violation investigation.<br><br><b>35,000 Affected Clients:</b> Personal data (names, national IDs, addresses, loan amounts) was exposed. Clients are panicking. Media is asking questions.<br><br><b>Law Enforcement:</b> FBI advises against paying ransomware. Filing with local prosecutors and Interpol is expected but unlikely to result in arrests.<br><br>Decide how quickly to notify the regulator and how much to invest in client communication and legal defense.`,
                    round3_budget_label: `Client Communication Budget ($K)`,
                    round3_budget_hint:  `Range: $50K to $500K. Covers client notification, credit monitoring, and hotline.`,
                    round3_strategy_label: `Regulator Notification Timing`,
                    round3_opt1: "Immediate — notify within 24 hours, with a partial picture",
                    round3_opt2: "Within 48 hours — notify at the regulator’s deadline",
                    round3_opt3: "After 72 hours — notify once the forensic picture is complete",

                    round4_briefing:     `<b>BUILDING CYBER RESILIENCE</b><br><br>The immediate crisis is contained. Now the board demands a comprehensive cybersecurity overhaul to prevent future attacks.<br><br><b>Available investments:</b><br>• Cloud backup with 4-hour RPO: $50K/year<br>• Data encryption at rest: $100K implementation<br>• Multi-factor authentication: $50K<br>• Network segmentation (DMZ): $150K<br>• 24/7 Security Operations Center: $100K/year<br>• Incident Response Plan: $30K<br>• Employee security training: $20K/year<br><br><b>Cyber Insurance Options:</b><br>• Basic: $90K/year — covers up to $3M<br>• Comprehensive: $180K/year — covers up to $5M<br><br>The board meets on 14 July. Allocate your security budget and choose insurance coverage.`,
